</tbody></table></div><p>Review <a href="/services/outsourced-sdr/">CallTeam outsourced SDR services</a> for the delivery scope and <a href="/human-led-appointment-setting/">human-led appointment setting</a> for responsibility inside the conversation. Owning a CRM record and having unrestricted rights to licensed data are not the same thing; settle both in the agreement.</p></div></section>

<section class="mp-section" id="shortlist"><div class="mp-wrap"><div class="mp-heading"><p class="mp-kicker">03 / Find the right service model</p><h2>Which memoryBlue alternative<br>belongs in your comparison?</h2><p>These are options to investigate, not performance rankings. Ask each provider to respond to the same campaign brief.</p></div><div class="gp-grid-two">
<article class="gp-tile gp-provider"><p class="gp-provider-label">CallTeam / a focused calling campaign</p><h3>Connect outreach to your sellers.</h3><p>Consider CallTeam when you need account preparation, human calling, follow-up, qualification and usable handoff managed around a specific B2B offer.</p><p>Supply a clear market, approved evidence and sellers ready to progress conversations. Review <a href="/services/b2b-appointment-setting/">appointment-setting scope</a> and the <a href="/pricing/">published starting assumptions</a>.</p></article>
<article class="gp-tile gp-provider"><p class="gp-provider-label">SalesHive / configurable SDR plans</p><h3>Compare location and channel options.</h3><p>SalesHive describes custom-quoted US-based or offshore SDR plans, with phone-only and phone-plus-email configurations. The selected plan determines capacity and commercial terms.</p><p><a href="https://saleshive.com/pricing/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Review official SalesHive plans ↗</a>. Our <a href="/compare/saleshive-alternatives/">SalesHive versus CallTeam comparison</a> goes deeper on that purchase.</p></article>
<article class="gp-tile gp-provider"><p class="gp-provider-label">SalesRoads / dedicated SDR programmes</p><h3>Assess the assigned team and support.</h3><p>SalesRoads publishes dedicated SDR programme pricing with supporting delivery infrastructure. It bills in four-week periods; account for that when comparing costs.</p><p><a href="https://salesroads.com/pricing/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Review official SalesRoads pricing ↗</a>. Confirm current staffing, inclusions and contractual terms.</p></article>
<article class="gp-tile gp-provider"><p class="gp-provider-label">Belkins / package-specific outreach</p><h3>Match the channels to the package.</h3><p>Belkins offers appointment-setting packages with manual research and different channel inclusions. Its small-business option can use partner-agency delivery.</p><p><a href="https://belkins.io/pricing" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Review official Belkins packages ↗</a>. Ask who will operate the selected work and which channels are included.</p></article>
</div><div class="mp-route-note"><p><strong>Keep memoryBlue on the shortlist when its model fits.</strong> Its wider service mix or available hiring pathway may suit a brief beyond a focused calling campaign. If your real need is permanent internal capability, compare hiring and management costs too.</p></div></div></section>

<section class="mp-section mp-paper" id="complete-cost"><div class="mp-wrap mp-split"><div><p class="mp-kicker">04 / Turn the quote into a comparable decision</p><h2>The headline fee does not<br>describe the whole purchase.</h2><p>Put the same target market, channels and workload into every brief. Separate service fees, onboarding, prospect research, data licences, tools and work your own people still perform.</p><ul class="gp-checklist"><li>Confirm how many people and which responsibilities are assigned.</li><li>Define a qualified meeting and how disputes or no-shows are handled.</li><li>Agree CRM updates, access, permitted data use and exports.</li><li>Record the billing period, minimum commitment and cancellation conditions.</li><li>Identify who handles discovery, proposals and closing after the handoff.</li></ul><p>Four-week and calendar-month billing are different periods. Over 52 weeks, thirteen four-week periods and twelve monthly charges need different arithmetic. The contract determines the actual obligation.</p></div><aside class="mp-tool"><p class="mp-label">Before choosing a provider</p><h3>Put the proposals<br>beside the same brief.</h3><p>The comparison tool helps organize costs, assigned work and unresolved questions. Use quoted figures rather than invented competitor rates.</p><a class="mp-button" href="/lead-generation-proposal-comparison/">Compare Your Agency Proposals ↗</a><p class="mp-small">Still defining the work? Prepare a <a href="/b2b-lead-generation-rfp-template/">Lead Generation Agency Brief</a> first.</p></aside></div></section>

